course: dictionary
lesson: 8473
title: Salute: a sign of respect or praise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word salute can be an action, a sign, or a way of praising someone. Use the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «The soldiers saluted the flag at dawn.» Here salute is an action: the soldiers raise a hand to their forehead to show respect.
explain: «We salute our volunteers.» No hand is raised here. To salute someone can mean to praise them openly for something brave or good. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Praise would fit, so that is the meaning.
explain: Salute can also be a formal word for greeting someone. Whichever meaning you choose, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: To salute means to raise your right hand to your forehead as a sign of respect, as soldiers do.
fact: A salute is that movement, or another sign of respect, such as a 21-gun salute, when guns are fired into the air.
fact: To salute someone can also mean to praise them openly for something brave or good.
fact: «I salute you» often means «well done, I admire you».
exercise: «The soldiers saluted the flag at dawn.» What does saluted mean here? | Sang a loud song | *Raised a hand to the forehead as a sign of respect | Ran around the flagpole
exercise: «We salute our volunteers for their hard work.» What does salute mean here? | Ask for a lift home | Forget | *Praise openly | Hide from
exercise: «The cannon gave a 21-gun salute.» What is a salute in this sentence? | *A sign of respect, shown by firing guns | A kind of soup | A loud argument | A type of lunch
test: Mum says «I salute you» when I finish my hard maths homework. What does she mean? | Please go away | You are late | *Well done, I admire you | I am hungry
test: «The soldiers are saluting as the hero comes.» What is happening? | The soldiers are running away | The soldiers are cooking a meal | *The soldiers are showing respect to the hero | The soldiers are asleep
exam: Which meaning of salute fits «The guard saluted the officer at the gate»? | *Raised a hand to the forehead as a sign of respect | To sing a song | To praise someone for a brave deed | To lose a game
